# Distributed Database Standards

Enforcement: **B**. Engine files refine this.

## Core ideas

- Data is partitioned; choose keys for locality of common transactions.
- Cross-partition transactions are more expensive — minimize them.
- Consistency and latency trade off with geography; state the requirement.
- Schema changes must consider rolling clusters and online DDL limitations.
- Hot spots (monotonic keys, low-cardinality partitions) cause pain — design around them.

## Checklist for schema work

- Partition / primary key rationale
- Expected transaction touch-set (single partition vs multi)
- Secondary index cost in a distributed setting
- Online migration approach and rollback limits
- Regional survivability assumptions (verify against actual deployment)
